\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces FBTS feature interpretability mapping. For each frequency band, the 17$\times $17 symmetric matrix shows how frequently each channel pair $(i,j)$ was selected among the top-100 features across 23 subjects and 5-fold CV. Theta (4--8\,Hz) and Beta (14--31\,Hz) dominate the feature selection, consistent with their established roles as drowsiness and alertness markers respectively. Diagonal entries represent channel variance; off-diagonal entries represent inter-channel covariance (functional connectivity).}}{13}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fbts_conn}{{6}{13}{FBTS feature interpretability mapping. For each frequency band, the 17$\times $17 symmetric matrix shows how frequently each channel pair $(i,j)$ was selected among the top-100 features across 23 subjects and 5-fold CV. Theta (4--8\,Hz) and Beta (14--31\,Hz) dominate the feature selection, consistent with their established roles as drowsiness and alertness markers respectively. Diagonal entries represent channel variance; off-diagonal entries represent inter-channel covariance (functional connectivity)}{figure.6}{}}
